C23 branch
==========

This branch supports #elifdef, #elifndef, #warning and #embed, plus binary
integer literals, digit separators, wb/WB integer suffixes, u8 character
constants and true/false in preprocessing expressions.

Macro expansion uses preprocessing tokens and implements function-like and
variadic macros, including __VA_ARGS__, __VA_OPT__, argument prescan,
stringification, token pasting, empty arguments and placemarkers, and
rescanning with recursive expansion suppression. Conditional expressions are
expanded before their operators are parsed. Include and line directive
arguments use the same expansion engine; symbol expansion and explanation
commands share it as well. --max-expansion controls the expansion size limit
(4K by default).

Coan remains a conditional-compilation analysis tool: it preserves ordinary
source text and does not read included headers or embed resource bytes.
Target-dependent __has_include, __has_embed and __has_c_attribute queries
remain unresolved, including with --implicit, unless explicitly configured
with -D or -U. GNU named variadics and the GNU comma-swallowing ## extension
are not implemented; use standard variadics and __VA_OPT__.

Build from Git with Autoconf 2.73+, Automake, and a C++11 or newer compiler:

    ./autogen.sh
    mkdir build && cd build
    ../configure
    make -j
    make check

The tests require Python 3. The C23/macro suite also compares expansions with
a C23-capable C compiler, selected by CPP (default: cc). For example:

    CPP=clang make check

